  "conclusion": "PASS for these three archived homogeneous Si acquisitions: the changed scalar overlap can be recomposed from stored coherent and tail fractions without rerunning multislice, to the precision of archived float64 arrays.",
  "method": "Independent calculation using the unchanged legacy virtual_density_at_scan evaluator and new physical-envelope helper. Recover each conditional coherent detector population W_i=C_old_i/[available*(1-P*d_old)], recover tail transport coefficients K_i=T_old_i/(available*d_old), and independently form available*[(1-P*d_new)*W_i+d_new*K_i]. Recover the uncollected coherent population after separately removing pre-sample loss and old tail loss. Check all arrays, budget, export encoding and recorded source hashes. The correction script itself was not executed during this review.",
  "population_formulae": {
    "available": "incident_fraction*tracked_fraction",
    "coherent": "available*(1-P*d)*W_i",
    "tail": "available*d*K_i",
    "uncollected": "pre_sample_loss + available*((1-P*d)*W_uncollected + d*(P-sum(K_i)))",
    "absorbed": "unchanged",
    "truncated": "old_truncated*(1-P*d_new)/(1-P*d_old); already part of uncollected, not an extra budget population"
  },
  "scope_and_limits": [
    "Only the scalar finite-envelope overlap changed; specimen wave potentials, phase, frozen configurations, grid, incident beam, retained tail angular law, physical detector routing and optical settings were reused unchanged.",
    "All tested probe centres are deep inside the homogeneous 10 nm disk. The legacy density was exactly the Gaussian-filtered raster support; the actual envelope overlap is numerically one.",
    "Old overlap and old coherent scale must be strictly positive for this inversion. This does not authorize reconstruction of arbitrary older frames without sufficient provenance, nonuniform material, zero-density locations or changed optical/sample physics.",
    "Corrected images retain the original acquisition lens strengths and DPA diameter 0.2 mm. They are not a new acquisition under the enlarged DPA or the new underfocus setting.",
    "PNG is flipped vertically to display minimum sample Y at the bottom; TIFF preserves raw row order and declares row_zero=minimum sample Y.",
    "The validation does not establish convergence or experimental accuracy of the retained multislice/Rutherford models. No new 64x64 wave propagation was run."
